node_modules/
.server.log

# The root .gitignore's diagnostic-render patterns were once UNANCHORED, so they matched at
# any depth and silently swallowed one vendored Cesium asset:
# public/vendor/cesium/Assets/Textures/maki/land-use.png. A 394-of-395 vendor would have
# committed clean and passed unnoticed. Those patterns are now anchored to the repository
# root, which is the real fix; this re-include stays as a belt against the next unanchored
# pattern somebody adds, since a partial vendor fails silently by nature.
!public/vendor/**
